      "extract": "In the Euclidean space Rn, log-concave measures, namely measures whose density is of the form e−U with U being a convex potential are known to satisfy several concentration inequalities. For instance, if a probability measure ν is absolutely continuous with respect to the standard Gaussian measure γ on Rn, with a corresponding density dν = eV dγ where the potential V : Rn →R satisﬁes the condition ∇2V ⪯(1 −δ)In, (1)",
